    "category": "test",
    "evidence": "Running _generated(seed, 2000) for seeds 1..40 (79,859 cases) gives 5 misses outside the D16 comma residual whose ending is a real TLD: seed 1 'refunds-portal \u2022 \u104aiv\uab32/claim', seed 4 'refunds-portal . \u104aoan/claim' and 'refunds-portal ~ \u104aive', seed 6 'refunds-portal \u2022 1 0' (2 further misses use 'claim', which is not in _TLDS). For 'Claim your energy rebate refund at refunds-portal ~ \u104aive before the deadline.' has_link_or_contact is False, SY.verify(...[1]) keeps the claim, and surface.clean shows it unmasked. Cause: _is_punct treats U+104A MYANMAR SIGN LITTLE SECTION (a confusables-listed look-alike of 'l') as punctuation because its script is in _SCRIPTS, so '\u104aive' splits into '' + 'ive' and is judged plain writing, contrary to D31 'every token is ordinary writing'. Not blocking only because D30 makes further look-alike variants owner-accepted residual.",
